From: Jonas Karlman <jonas@kwiboo.se>
Subject: [PATCH] media: rkvdec: reset controls, pm-runtime and QoS fixes (6.18 rebase)

Rebased on Linux 6.18 (rkvdec moved out of staging to
drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec). Squash of:

  - WIP: media: rkvdec: pm runtime dont use autosuspend before (Jonas Karlman <jonas@kwiboo.se>)
  - soc: rockchip: power-domain: export idle request (Randy Li <ayaka@soulik.info>)
  - WIP: media: rkvdec: implement reset controls (Alex Bee <knaerzche@gmail.com>)
  - WIP: arm64: dts: add resets to vdec for RK3399 (Alex Bee <knaerzche@gmail.com>)
  - media: hantro: rockchip: Increase RK3288's max ACLK (Alex Bee <knaerzche@gmail.com>)
  - media: rkvdec: disable QoS for VP9 (corruptions on RK3328 (Alex Bee <knaerzche@gmail.com>)
  - WIP: arm64: dts: add resets to vdec for RK3328 (Alex Bee <knaerzche@gmail.com>)

Origin: Batocera/LibreELEC "rkvdec" series by Jonas Karlman, Randy Li and Alex Bee (originals: Signed-off-by lines below);
        rebased onto Linux 6.18 and squashed by REG-Linux.

Signed-off-by: Jonas Karlman <jonas@kwiboo.se>
Signed-off-by: Caesar Wang <wxt@rock-chips.com>
Signed-off-by: Jeffy Chen <jeffy.chen@rock-chips.com>
Signed-off-by: Randy Li <ayaka@soulik.info>
Signed-off-by: Alex Bee <knaerzche@gmail.com>
[Romain Tisserand: rebased on 6.18 and squashed]
Signed-off-by: Romain Tisserand <romain.tisserand@gmail.com>
